NEWS.md:3789:* `confint()` now applies the small-sample t(g - 1) width plus the simulation-calibrated `log(g/(g - 1))` centre shift by default for location-axis structured random-effect SD targets. This moves only the phylo and relmat bivariate q2 `mu1:x`/`mu2:x` slope SD cells to `inference_ready` for interval and coverage status; `supported` remains withheld because the engine grids still measure right-tail miss asymmetry and g-dependence. Spatial q2, animal q2, q4/q8, count, and non-Gaussian structured rows remain separate future arcs.
